WEBVTT

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:01.980
Yakitate!! 9!

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:03.390
The third match was to be held at
the city of Saito in Miyazaki prefecture.

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:05.070
City of Saito, Miyazaki Prefecture

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:08.110
With perfectly ripe mangoes as the specialty product,

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:11.030
the match against CMAP began.

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:11.320
<b>3 pieces</b>

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:12.620
Whoa!

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.030
7000 yen for just three pieces?!

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:26.250
Ooo, mango!

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.470
Could this be a reaction to the ripe mango?

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:29.750
A kanchou mango?!

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:37.260
Ooo, mango!

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.400
I don’t believe this.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.310
There’s an idiot having a reaction in this kind of place.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:46.940
Say, Kaname...

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:49.900
Did Tsubodzuka really lose to these idiots?

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.570
Well, so it seems.

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:54.660
God, that Tsubodzuka...

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.080
He really is scum.

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:58.030
Kinda want him to die, right?

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:02.790
Yeah, and we don’t even know what he means when he uses those foreign words...

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:06.380
Kazuma could not forgive the members of CMAP

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:08.590
for even insulting their former member, Tsubodzuka.

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:12.180
He vows to win against them at all
costs with his specialty, the <i>Japan</i>.

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:15.970
However, if you look at what’s
happening after the match began...

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:17.260
Exactly.

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:21.810
They’re probably using demiglace sauce
made from Miyazaki beef.

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:22.980
Miyazaki beef?

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:26.860
This is what you do to create the
curry bread of the highest quality.

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:28.820
And, look carefully.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:31.150
The technique that Narumi guy’s using...

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:33.360
It’s as though he’s painting a picture on water...

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.490
He’s mixing it slowly and gently.

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:40.030
That’s the movement of a person who’s mastered western cooking!

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:42.540
It’s known as “Tuning the Iron Pot”!

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:44.710
How stupid.

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:49.300
No matter what talent you fellows may have,
you cannot win against Azuma.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:54.550
He has a natural gift that surpasses
even me, a genius of a commander.

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:56.550
Then, let me ask you this.

00:01:56.550 --> 00:02:01.050
Do you know that you shouldn’t add
fruit juice directly to bread dough?

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:02.810
Of course I do!

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:04.270
If you do something like that,

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:07.690
the proteases in the fruit juice will
digest the gluten of the dough,

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:10.320
and you won’t be able to knead it.

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:12.650
Just as you’d expect of the commander.

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:13.320
However...

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:16.450
That guy... just added it to the dough.

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:19.320
Fruit juice that hasn’t been boiled at all, straight.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:22.830
What was that?!

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:30.000
Oh, the dough’s all melted.

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:34.340
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:36.130
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:38.430
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:42.020
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:47.060
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:51.030
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:02:55.150 --> 00:03:01.580
I want this voice to reach you, even though it’s still a tiny song.

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:07.750
That’s because I have the feeling that something’s gonna start.

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:22.850
As I was cowering, muffling my voice, the tears that I shed

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:31.440
probably helped me notice that

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:37.320
I’ve almost forgotten how to believe.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:46.210
The future that I painted (I will fulfill it)

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:51.580
Looking up to the clear skies,

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:58.720
I begin to run once again. Someday, I want to dye

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:04.510
that white sky with my colors.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:11.520
I’m going to fly as far as possible, shining like a marble,

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:15.900
unfolding these wings of mine.

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:24.590
Love will rescue Saito as well!!

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:27.390
The Solar Hands vs. The Flame Arm!

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:30.200
Wait just a moment, you numskull!

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.830
What’s wrong?

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:35.720
You’ve done your job well, Kawachi...

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:38.220
So, it’s all right to relax with the audience.

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:39.230
Are you a moron...?

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:41.440
This is no time to be saying that!!

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:44.190
If you were to put unprocessed juice straight into the dough,

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:46.690
the proteases in the juices would destroy the gluten,

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:48.800
leaving you unable to knead the dough.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:51.820
Didn’t you even know that?!

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:53.350
Of course I knew that.

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:55.850
It’d turn out like this, right?

00:04:57.370 --> 00:04:59.160
During the newcomers’ battle,

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:01.230
Yukino put those weird enzymes into your dough.

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:05.040
You think that after seeing how hard a time you had,

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:07.370
I wouldn’t know something like this?

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:09.380
But... But then...

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:10.380
I did this on purpose.

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:10.870
Huh?

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:14.120
Don’t worry, I’m doing this on purpose.

00:05:14.470 --> 00:05:15.790
On purpose...?

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:20.860
I wonder if it’s really all right...

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:23.800
So how was it, Mr. Genius Commander?

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:28.000
Were you sure to explain the
basics of breadmaking to him?

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.650
Of course I explained it to him.

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:34.980
My ultimate technique that can
convert this pinch into an opportunity!

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:37.460
U-Ultimate technique?!

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:39.080
Oh?

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:40.540
And what might that...?

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:42.370
That, you see, is...

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:43.160
You an idiot?!

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:46.450
I can’t tell our opponent something like that!

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:49.130
Geez, what’s he trying to get out of me?

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:53.880
I mean, even I don’t know what Azuma’s trying, so...

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:56.890
I couldn’t possibly tell him anything even if I wanted to.

00:05:56.890 --> 00:05:58.470
An amazing bluff.

00:05:58.470 --> 00:05:59.420
Yeah.

00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:03.570
Well, it can’t be helped if you
really don’t want to talk about it.

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:06.130
However, burn this into your brain.

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:10.320
Our breadmaking is ultimate on top of perfect.

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:14.720
Like we’d care about some stupid bread made
by someone who doesn’t even know the basics!

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:16.320
What was that?!

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:18.730
If you think that was a lie, then let me explain it to you in greater detail.

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:21.230
First, that fellow Chimatsuri’s skill...

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:25.240
Chimatsuri is made such that he
doesn’t sweat no matter how hot a day it is.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:31.170
Even on a hot day like this, his
body temperature keeps rising.

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:35.200
The temperature of his arm surpasses even that of the Solar Hands.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:37.430
It becomes a Flame Arm!

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:39.720
H-How could that be?!

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:41.600
It surpasses even the Solar Hands?!

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:44.750
Secondly, my ultimate technique...

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:48.230
Look carefully at the powder that Chimatsuri’s
sprinkling on the completed dough.

00:06:48.230 --> 00:06:48.940
All right.

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:49.980
That should do it.

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:52.820
Wh-What is that powder?

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:56.320
If you add a powder to curry bread,
it has to be breadcrumbs, right?

00:06:56.320 --> 00:06:59.190
That happens to be finely ground cornflakes.

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:03.620
Unlike breadcrumbs, cornflakes don’t absorb oil as easily.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:06.290
Moreover, it has a crisp texture and is fragrant.

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:08.690
Therefore, the end product is truly fantastic.

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:11.210
Is... Is that so...?

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:14.710
This is a commonly used
technique at high-end bakeries.

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:17.890
Don’t tell me that you didn’t know of it?

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:20.850
Everyone knows at least that much.

00:07:20.850 --> 00:07:21.960
Liar.

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:26.770
Cornflakes are an item that can be
easily made in a regular household.

00:07:26.770 --> 00:07:33.690
Earlier, I had Narumi make some
with Saito’s highest-quality corn.

00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:36.740
As a cook, Narumi’s skill is magnificent.

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:39.900
Even if it’s just making cornflakes, he’s a genius.

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:42.400
Th... These guys are perfect.

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:45.290
Even though they hate each other,

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:49.210
the pivotal commander is able to bring out
everyone’s potential to the fullest.

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:50.700
In comparison to that...

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:52.340
Hold on!

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:54.920
The dough is spilling onto the floor, Azuma-kun.

00:07:54.920 --> 00:07:56.300
Sorry about that.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:59.300
I’m just not used to handling
dough that’s in liquid state like this.

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:01.090
They’re still fooling around.

00:08:01.090 --> 00:08:03.310
I hate to admit it, but it looks
like this time we’re done for.

00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:04.790
So, you understand now?

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:08.390
In the end, your skill and talent
are all there is to cooking.

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:12.360
It’s ten years too early for scum like you to be winning against us.

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:17.930
Wh-What’s that helicopter?

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:23.370
It looks like the Goddess who’s
bringing in our victory has arrived, too.

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:25.200
Here you go!

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:27.160
CMAP’s special curry bread.

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:28.460
All done.

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:30.440
Eat it quickly, while it’s still warm.

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:33.220
Very well, then.

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:47.770
Th-This is delicious.

00:08:47.770 --> 00:08:49.390
A wonderful curry bread.

00:08:49.390 --> 00:08:51.730
In addition to the dough being firm and springy,

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:54.060
the cornflakes sprinkled on the surface are...

00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:57.530
Well, it looks like he’s praising it, but...

00:08:57.530 --> 00:09:00.390
How very uninspired.
There’s no reaction.

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:03.620
What a pity...

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:08.650
It looks like your bread couldn’t
meet up to Kuro-yan’s high standards...

00:09:11.830 --> 00:09:13.290
What’s this animal?!

00:09:13.290 --> 00:09:15.590
He’s turned into some strange sort of animal!

00:09:15.590 --> 00:09:19.050
My glasses were stolen by a strange animal!

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:22.130
Wh-What in the world is this?!

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:23.290
Don’t you know...?

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:25.500
What this lovely little animal is?

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:30.180
This animal inhabits an area from Myanmar to
Thailand, as well as the Malaysian peninsula.

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:34.310
A mammal and an odd-toed ungulate, popularly known as the Malay tapir!

00:09:34.310 --> 00:09:35.180
Malay tapir?!]

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:37.680
Try saying “Malay tapir” ten times in a row.

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:39.800
Say it quickly.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:45.700
Malay tapir.

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:47.910
And... what was the bread that I just ate?

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:49.070
Malay tapir!

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:54.570
It’s curry bread!

00:09:57.590 --> 00:10:00.090
C-Curry bread and Malay tapir...

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:03.080
Though they may be similar,
they’re really quite different...

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:07.550
To think that he brought that weird
animal here, just for his reaction...

00:10:07.550 --> 00:10:10.520
It means that their curry bread’s the real things.

00:10:10.520 --> 00:10:12.350
That’s not all, Kawachi-san.

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:13.520
What was that?!

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:14.230
Huh?

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:17.090
Hey... That’s not me...

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:19.980
Here.

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:21.680
Oh, thank you.

00:10:21.990 --> 00:10:22.650
Huh?

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:23.950
Who might you be...?

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:25.160
So, what is it?!

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:30.740
Actually, the Miyazaki prefecture
zoo doesn’t have a Malay tapir.

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:32.560
So, what about that?

00:10:34.370 --> 00:10:35.700
D-Don’t tell me...

00:10:36.170 --> 00:10:37.710
Have you figured it out yet?

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:38.710
That’s right.

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:43.200
That Malay tapir was flown in,
all the way from another prefecture.

00:10:43.510 --> 00:10:44.590
What was that?!

00:10:44.590 --> 00:10:48.710
The helicopter that you saw earlier was carrying the tapir.

00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:54.550
This is the victorious reaction that befits the perfect bread that we made!

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:58.440
H-How can this be...?

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:01.720
To think that their bread’s evaluation was so high...

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:04.030
Perhaps it’s just like Kaname said....

00:11:04.030 --> 00:11:06.720
Cooking’s simply a matter of skill and talent.

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:07.950
But...

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:09.730
But...

00:11:10.410 --> 00:11:13.250
I still have a faint hope.

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:16.540
I’ll definitely crush them with my <i>Japan</i>!

00:11:16.540 --> 00:11:21.030
I believe in your soul, from when you swore that you’d definitely crush these guys,

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:23.700
to protect Tsubodzuka’s honor!

00:11:24.090 --> 00:11:24.870
All right.

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:26.330
Baking’s complete!

00:11:31.260 --> 00:11:32.920
What in the world is that bread...?

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:51.440
All right.

00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:52.870
It’s done!

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:54.190
Mister Kuroyanagi!

00:11:54.490 --> 00:11:55.810
Th-That’s...

00:11:58.330 --> 00:11:59.650
A haniwa?

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:01.250
I see!

00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:04.800
He’s shaped it into Saito’s famed haniwa.

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:06.490
Yeah, looks like it.

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:08.680
Just as you’d expect of Azuma.

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:10.300
You’ve really thought it out.

00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:12.250
What are they, idiots?

00:12:13.310 --> 00:12:15.770
Kinda feels like they felt that
since they couldn’t win on taste alone,

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:17.480
they went for outward appearance.

00:12:17.480 --> 00:12:20.600
It’s hard to understand the
train of thought of these plebeians.

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:22.190
What’s with you guys?

00:12:22.190 --> 00:12:24.390
All three of you out here together now?

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:28.950
Sure beats twiddling our thumbs, with
you guys being so slow in breadmaking,

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:30.360
so we came to visit.

00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:33.240
Well, since you guys will be losing anyway...

00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:34.900
Just disappear already.

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:36.330
Try saying that again.

00:12:36.330 --> 00:12:38.070
Stop that, Kawachi.

00:12:38.460 --> 00:12:40.000
Don’t bother with them.

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:42.820
For now, just look over at Azuma’s battle.

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:45.050
Y-Yeah...

00:12:56.930 --> 00:12:59.600
While you may feel kinda sorry for it...

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:01.600
Press down on its mouth with your hands

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:03.420
and bite on the head with its eyes facing downwards as you’re eating it.

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:04.770
In other words...

00:13:04.770 --> 00:13:06.900
I should have it facing this way,

00:13:06.900 --> 00:13:09.820
and while pressing down on the haniwa’s mouth, I bite.

00:13:09.820 --> 00:13:11.140
Right?

00:13:11.860 --> 00:13:12.680
That’s right.

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:15.830
There’s soft uncooked mango inside,

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:19.370
so if you eat if like that, the mango
will only come out from the eyeholes.

00:13:19.370 --> 00:13:22.000
That way, it won’t squirt out all over the place.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:22.870
I see.

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:25.040
The mango is shut in airtight.

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:29.120
In order to prevent it from squirting out all over
the place, you came up with this strategy, eh?

00:13:29.590 --> 00:13:30.930
Impressive.

00:13:33.050 --> 00:13:35.520
What, you want to eat some, too?

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:38.670
Then, eat this.

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:42.300
I made one more, thinking of giving it to Kawachi later.

00:13:43.970 --> 00:13:45.930
Oh, thank you very much.

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:47.220
Thanks for letting him eat it.

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:48.140
No problem.

00:13:48.710 --> 00:13:50.390
Well then, let’s taste this.

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:51.100
Okay!

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:09.070
All right!

00:14:11.820 --> 00:14:15.580
Far from showing a reaction; he isn’t moving a finger!

00:14:16.570 --> 00:14:19.620
Did you poison him or something, because there wasn’t any hope of his winning?

00:14:20.030 --> 00:14:21.870
Murder is a crime, you know.

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:22.950
What are you, idiots?

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:23.870
Look carefully.

00:14:23.870 --> 00:14:25.050
Wh-What?

00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:35.010
Th-This is...

00:14:35.010 --> 00:14:36.590
It’s like a haniwa!

00:14:36.590 --> 00:14:38.230
The judge has frozen stiff!

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:41.100
This isn’t good...

00:14:41.890 --> 00:14:43.280
Don’t worry, guys.

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:46.060
It is possible that he’s pretending to be frozen stiff.

00:14:46.060 --> 00:14:47.900
But, there’s no acting in flying a tapir over.

00:14:48.440 --> 00:14:52.270
Our bread was so awesome, it
couldn’t be expressed with mere acting.

00:14:52.270 --> 00:14:54.070
Th-That’s right.

00:14:54.070 --> 00:14:55.320
Of course, that’s it.

00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:56.700
Yeah, that has to be it.

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:58.410
You really think so?

00:14:58.410 --> 00:14:59.870
Then, let me ask you...

00:15:00.530 --> 00:15:05.960
Do you think the tapir you guys are so
proud of is also pretending to be a haniwa?

00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:09.010
Tapir!

00:15:09.420 --> 00:15:11.250
Wh... What’s wrong?

00:15:11.250 --> 00:15:12.790
What’s happening?!

00:15:12.790 --> 00:15:15.130
Are they still alive?!

00:15:15.130 --> 00:15:16.470
Doctor!

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:19.390
Ah, is it my turn?

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:21.100
Let’s go, Dog!

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:27.990
Note: This is a parody of the manga “Wild Life.”

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:41.610
What is that?

00:15:41.610 --> 00:15:46.340
Isn’t that the weird vet who treated us on the
uninhabited island during the Monaco Cup?

00:15:48.040 --> 00:15:51.380
When did that dog get on top of Kawachi-san’s head?

00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:02.140
Is that someone you know?

00:16:03.090 --> 00:16:06.640
Well, yes and no...

00:16:06.640 --> 00:16:08.270
He just suddenly appeared in our anime.

00:16:08.270 --> 00:16:10.140
And he even treats humans here.

00:16:10.140 --> 00:16:11.560
It’s a weird veterinarian.

00:16:11.560 --> 00:16:12.940
Is that so?

00:16:12.940 --> 00:16:14.700
But, before that...

00:16:15.440 --> 00:16:17.730
Yeah, there’s nothing to worry about.

00:16:17.730 --> 00:16:18.990
He’s alive all right.

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:20.570
And the voice of his heart is in full working order.

00:16:20.570 --> 00:16:22.700
Th-The voice of his heart, you say?

00:16:22.700 --> 00:16:23.300
That’s right.

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:26.490
I have the power of absolute sense of sound,

00:16:26.490 --> 00:16:28.340
so I can hear such things, too.

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:31.040
Absolute sense of sound?

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:33.580
It seems like a completely useless talent...

00:16:33.580 --> 00:16:36.310
So, what is it that they’re saying?

00:16:36.310 --> 00:16:37.220
That’s...

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:39.850
The victor is... Pantasia!

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:41.420
All right!

00:16:41.420 --> 00:16:43.010
We did it, Azuma-kun!

00:16:43.010 --> 00:16:43.850
Yep!

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:45.970
That was wonderful.

00:16:45.970 --> 00:16:46.980
You did well.

00:16:47.350 --> 00:16:49.680
Just as you’d expect of Azuma and Kanmuri.

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:53.990
Well, I was certain you guys would win from the very beginning.

00:16:54.520 --> 00:16:55.560
Is that so?

00:16:55.560 --> 00:16:58.000
Has he completely forgotten about

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:01.500
when he stormed in shouting at Azuma while he was working?

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:04.240
How does this guy’s brain deal with these memories anyway?

00:17:04.240 --> 00:17:06.320
Regular people can’t possibly understand.

00:17:06.320 --> 00:17:08.700
Then again, it’s okay to not understand.

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:10.750
P-Please wait just one moment!

00:17:11.330 --> 00:17:12.710
What’s wrong, guys?

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:15.540
Don’t tell me that you’re arguing with the results at this point in time?

00:17:15.540 --> 00:17:16.880
Of course we are.

00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:19.750
We can’t possibly agree with such a judgment.

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:22.600
Also, what the hell’s with that veterinarian, anyway?

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:25.100
And what’s all this about the “voice of the heart”?

00:17:26.550 --> 00:17:29.050
Well, it’s true that even I find it a little hard to believe everything about him,

00:17:29.050 --> 00:17:31.780
including the “voice of the heart.”

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:33.520
This match is invalid.

00:17:33.520 --> 00:17:34.310
That’s right!
This match is invalid.

00:17:34.310 --> 00:17:35.520
Exactly!

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:37.030
All of you, just die already.

00:17:37.730 --> 00:17:39.480
Hey, you veterinarian there.

00:17:39.480 --> 00:17:42.780
If you can really hear the voice of the heart,

00:17:42.780 --> 00:17:46.160
then explain it in the judge’s stead
so that we can all understand.

00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:47.040
Very well.

00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:52.550
As long as the voice of his heart speaks,
I shall speak on his behalf.

00:17:53.200 --> 00:17:55.340
First, I must listen for the sound.

00:18:07.140 --> 00:18:08.400
All right, let’s do this, then.

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:14.730
In the first place, you guys don’t understand
the reason Azuma liquified his dough at all!

00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:16.980
That’s right!

00:18:16.980 --> 00:18:19.400
Even if we stop laughing about the voice of his heart,

00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:21.820
we still don’t know the reason behind that trick of Azuma’s.

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:24.690
That guy... just added it to the dough.

00:18:24.690 --> 00:18:27.330
Fruit juice that hasn’t been boiled at all, straight.

00:18:27.740 --> 00:18:31.120
Oh, the dough’s all melted.

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:34.720
If you just want to add the flavor of the juice to the dough,

00:18:34.720 --> 00:18:37.790
all you have to do is add heat-inactivated juice.

00:18:37.790 --> 00:18:39.930
So, why did he go to all the trouble of...?

00:18:41.880 --> 00:18:45.300
Azuma added fruit juice straight
into the dough on purpose.

00:18:45.300 --> 00:18:46.630
That is, in order to...

00:18:46.630 --> 00:18:48.670
create a bread with a new consistency, made with wheat flour,

00:18:48.670 --> 00:18:50.730
where the gluten has been broken down.

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:51.100
Gluten

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:52.480
It... It can’t be!
Gluten

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:52.940
It... It can’t be!

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:54.810
New Consistency

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:55.610
No way!
New Consistency

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:58.140
B... But it’s still weird!

00:18:58.140 --> 00:18:59.620
Leaving aside the new consistency,

00:18:59.620 --> 00:19:03.150
without gluten, the wheat flour would become like tempura flour!

00:19:03.150 --> 00:19:05.070
How could that possibly taste good?

00:19:05.070 --> 00:19:06.070
Yeah!

00:19:06.070 --> 00:19:08.580
You guys are really stupid, aren’t you?

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:12.370
That’s because there’s something called yeast in it!

00:19:12.370 --> 00:19:13.540
Y-Yeast?!

00:19:13.990 --> 00:19:18.540
Even if the gluten’s gone, the dough will
continue to ferment as long as the yeast’s inside.

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:21.510
That’s why if you were to put it in
a container and actually bake it...

00:19:23.630 --> 00:19:27.590
it’d have both the softness of a pancake
and the crispiness of tempura.

00:19:27.590 --> 00:19:29.680
You’d get yourself a bread-waffle!

00:19:29.680 --> 00:19:31.590
I-Is that so?!

00:19:31.590 --> 00:19:33.060
By the way...

00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:36.550
This taste is so good that if that fake Kansai boy there

00:19:37.930 --> 00:19:43.280
tried this at the time of the newcomers’ battle
instead of simply giving up, he’d have won.

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:45.230
Wh-What was that?!

00:19:45.230 --> 00:19:48.500
Wait, why do you even know something like that?!

00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:50.700
D-Dammit!

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:52.960
Why’d it have to turn out like this?!

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:53.530
No!

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:55.580
Everybody should just disappear!

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:56.290
No! No! No!

00:19:56.290 --> 00:19:58.880
Stop crying, will ya?!
No! No! No!

00:19:59.250 --> 00:20:00.170
Listen up!

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:02.340
What your bread completely lacked was...

00:20:03.040 --> 00:20:04.850
love.

00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:07.590
L-Love?!
Note: <b>愛 (“ai”) = love</b>

00:20:07.590 --> 00:20:09.350
That’s right, love.
Note: <b>愛 (“ai”) = love</b>

00:20:10.340 --> 00:20:11.550
Why do you think that Azuma

00:20:11.550 --> 00:20:17.360
used uncooked mango, and took the trouble
to make the bread into the shape of a haniwa?

00:20:18.560 --> 00:20:20.100
It was...

00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:21.740
for the sake of love.

00:20:22.310 --> 00:20:25.190
The love that the locals put into raising their mangoes,

00:20:25.190 --> 00:20:28.740
and the love that went into wanting to
make the local souvenirs more appealing...

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:31.750
That is what made this a great bread!

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:37.000
Love is what’ll save Saito!

00:20:39.290 --> 00:20:40.460
It’s our...

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:42.260
Complete loss.

00:20:42.870 --> 00:20:45.180
Well, as long as you understand that.

00:20:46.040 --> 00:20:47.130
Also...

00:20:47.130 --> 00:20:50.140
This is a present for you guys, from the tapir.

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:52.180
F... From the tapir?

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:53.130
Yeah.

00:20:53.130 --> 00:20:55.430
He wants you guys to taste
this bread that’s filled with love,

00:20:55.430 --> 00:20:59.150
to show his gratitude for bringing him here for the reaction.

00:20:59.600 --> 00:21:01.940
I cut it up with my scalpel.

00:21:06.860 --> 00:21:07.740
See ya.

00:21:08.570 --> 00:21:11.750
W... Well, I don’t quite get it, but...

00:21:12.240 --> 00:21:15.280
It appears that vet saved us.

00:21:15.280 --> 00:21:16.450
Yeah.

00:21:16.450 --> 00:21:20.590
However, I wonder if it’s all right for him to have left the dog here.

00:21:23.870 --> 00:21:26.540
I’m kinda worried about them.

00:21:26.540 --> 00:21:28.220
Why’s that?

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:33.050
In the end, after eating our bread, they also turned into haniwas...

00:21:33.050 --> 00:21:35.730
So, they probably won’t be suing us.

00:21:36.220 --> 00:21:39.230
That’s not what I’m worried about.

00:21:39.810 --> 00:21:42.980
I didn’t like them, but it’s not like
I had a grudge against them.

00:21:43.520 --> 00:21:47.450
Thinking about the possibility that they
may never be able to recover from this,

00:21:48.020 --> 00:21:49.440
I...

00:21:49.440 --> 00:21:52.490
You’re really kind.

00:21:53.030 --> 00:21:54.570
It’s all right.

00:21:55.240 --> 00:21:58.090
They’ve been living as entertainers since their childhoods.

00:21:58.830 --> 00:22:01.790
That’s why their hearts had become just a little twisted.

00:22:02.330 --> 00:22:04.590
But, now that they’ve turned into haniwas,

00:22:04.590 --> 00:22:07.040
by interacting with people in this way,

00:22:07.040 --> 00:22:11.510
I’m sure that the original kindness and love
that they possessed will return to them.

00:22:12.670 --> 00:22:13.520
That’s true...

00:22:14.050 --> 00:22:15.470
I’m sure of it.

00:22:15.470 --> 00:22:17.520
Yeah, definitely.

00:22:18.260 --> 00:22:19.850
Yep.

00:22:20.510 --> 00:22:21.770
I guess that’s how it’ll be!

00:22:21.770 --> 00:22:23.100
But, of course.

00:22:23.100 --> 00:22:24.820
Yep, yep.

00:22:27.150 --> 00:22:29.860
All’s well that ends well then.

00:22:30.730 --> 00:22:32.700
I wonder if it’ll really end so well...

00:22:53.930 --> 00:23:02.230
The world will probably go on today, with a repetition of the same faces,

00:23:02.230 --> 00:23:10.280
but there was one thing that I’d forgotten.

00:23:10.700 --> 00:23:15.050
If I’m to take a deep breath,

00:23:15.050 --> 00:23:19.040
then the shape of the love that permeates my surroundings

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:26.630
will shine so much that it’s blinding.

00:23:27.010 --> 00:23:35.010
Someone is calling me from far away...

00:23:35.390 --> 00:23:43.400
And that voice constantly echoes in my heart.

00:23:43.610 --> 00:23:51.990
So, riding on my small pleasures, the merry-go-round begins to turn...

00:23:51.990 --> 00:24:02.540
And even on days when the morning doesn’t come, it shines a light in my heart.

00:24:05.880 --> 00:24:07.650
Today it’s idols, tomorrow it’s ninjas!

00:24:07.650 --> 00:24:08.970
Am I gonna be a kunoichi or something?!

00:24:09.570 --> 00:24:11.380
If ninjas are involved, does that mean...?!

00:24:11.380 --> 00:24:15.110
No! Whatever you do, don’t mention that one ninja anime!

00:24:15.110 --> 00:24:16.660
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan:

00:24:16.660 --> 00:24:19.060
Nin Nin Nin!! My Way of the Ninja!!

00:24:19.060 --> 00:24:19.970
Be sure to watch!

00:24:20.450 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:22.730 --> 00:24:26.520
The Malay tapir has the largest body of all tapirs.

00:24:26.520 --> 00:24:29.240
It lives in areas close to water bodies such as rivers and lakes.

00:24:29.240 --> 00:24:31.150
It is very good at swimming and diving under water.

00:24:31.150 --> 00:24:31.750
Tapir!

00:24:31.750 --> 00:24:33.500
Tapirs!
